 "question": "How would you insert 5 into this binary search tree? Show the comparisons, where 5 ends up, and the in-order traversal afterwards.",
 "reference_answer": "Start at the root 8: 5 < 8, go left to 3. 5 > 3, go right to 6. 5 < 6, go left to 4. 5 > 4 and 4 has no right child, so 5 becomes the right child of 4 (a new leaf; path 8 -> 3 -> 6 -> 4). In-order traversal afterwards: 1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 10, 13, 14 (sorted).",
